body:
Right now, the getConfiguration works on plain objects. Those plain objects are then merged into a single object.

This way of doing has several issues: 
- Its usage rely on knowing the internal structure of the `SearchParameters`
- the merge is naive, which leads to issues
- the user has poor control on the application of his changes

Buuuut `SearchParameters` have a nice and friendly API. So what about this API:

``` js
getConfiguration(SearchParameters, stateFromTheURL) => SearchParameters
```

When implementing a widget this would look like: 

``` js
search.addWidget({
  getConfiguration: function(searchParams, url) {
    return searchParams.addFacet('myFacet');
  }
});
```

Bonus: in the same spirit of giving more power / responsability to the implementors, maybe it should be their responsability to merge what comes from the URL?
